{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1348003-the-headcanon-thread","id":1348003,"title":"The Headcanon Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-12T13:46:57-08:00","id":1348003,"title":"The Headcanon Thread","content":"So every CofD fan probably has their own interpretation of the setting which is not supported by canon at best and outright contradicting it at worst. As I think that hearing what other ways people expand/ change in their versions of the setting is interesting, and Exalted has a similar thread, I thought why to not start a similar one for our own, dark world. So if anyone has some facts and tidbits about the game which they would like to share, this would be the place to do so, so just feel free to share your ideas about any of the CofD's games!<br /> <br /> Here are few examples-<br /> <br /> - the Contagion is not a disease as much as it is a curse. Or more exactly, curses. The First Children from the Testament of the Pain Prophet? Each of the survivors had the ability to lay a terrible curse upon mankind, and each such curse is yet another strain of the Contagion- and as not everyone has used their curses, we may have some new and terrible times waiting to happen upon us.<br /> <br /> - the Black Sun Map is actually a thing. It is, in fact, the &quot;blueprints of the God Machine&quot;. If one were to complete it, they could access the Command and Control Infrastructures if the God Machine and reprogram it to stop maintaining the status que and actually do something.<br /> <br /> - once every five years, the leaders of all hunter conspiracies and most important compacts gather together in a lone castle in Prague. They have dinner together, exchange some information, drink some wine, have laughs and then return home. Network Zero are not invited.<br /> <br /> - unlike many other dead things, vampires still have a soul. It is just trapped in their body in the moment of death, and slowly decays into its elements. The remains of the soul, or the &quot;decayed part&quot; is the Beast- so when the soul is rotten completely, only the Beast remains, hence becoming a Draugr. <br /> <br /> I'll a few others later. Feel free to add your own!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T14:08:03-08:00","id":1348010,"title":"","content":"is this for each gameline, our own settings with only some of the gamelines being canon, or a very crowded &quot;every gameline is here&quot; Chroniclesverse?<br /> <br /> Edit: finally thought of a couple.<br /> <br /> The soul has multiple parts just like Mummy said, corresponding to something like the five Egyptian portions of the soul. From memory: The Shadow, The True Name, The Ba (seat of personality), The Heart (your emotional capacity) and Life Force. Mages only deal with a portion of the soul with death magic, but there are secret arts that use all five arcana to mess with the entire soul. What happens when you mess with that? ask the Demons<br /> <br /> Souls, or at least part of them, used to be the Spirits of Homo Habilis or some other pre-human ancestor. At some point, after millions of years of Claimings, they underwent a process similar to what happened with the mitochondria and chloroplasts and became near-mindless endosymbionts. They got a regular source of human-flavored Essence and humans got both the anti-possession defense system known as Integrity and perhaps even the ability to be transformed into the splats. The fact that they are interchangeable between people is the last remnant of their independent nature, as they can survive on any Human Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 11-12-2019, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T14:11:13-08:00","id":1348012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1348003-the-headcanon-thread?p=1348010#post1348010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is this for each gameline, our own settings with only some of the gamelines being canon, or a very crowded &quot;every gameline is here&quot; Chroniclesverse?</div> </div> </div> </div>All of the above :P (that is, no crossover is required, nor it is forbidden)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T14:33:54-08:00","id":1348017,"title":"","content":"More of them. <br /> <br /> Luna can still cause Ghouls to undergo the First Change, as she is the Goddess of Change and the stasis of Vitae means nothing to her.<br /> <br /> All of Acrozatarim's work is canon. All of it.<br /> <br /> All of LostLight and TheKingsRavens Jewish and Israeli Hunter Orgs are canon. <br /> <br /> Horrors can be shaped into replicas of the public image of particularly infamous non-Beast Apexes. Whoever is Devoured by this horror gains unbreakable Family Ties with that person, even if they are a Demon or even entirely mundane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T14:59:00-08:00","id":1348024,"title":"","content":"I have a few, but my two big ones are these:<ul><li>Prometheans are pulled &quot;up&quot; from the Lower Depths in a parallel fashion how Mages are &quot;pulled up&quot; into the Supernal. This is why the Created cause Disquiet and Wasteland, why they don't have a soul, and why Pandorans are just so damn hungry.</li> <li>Just as there are a multitude of beings you can call &quot;angels&quot; or &quot;demons,&quot; there are a handful of different types of &quot;ghosts&quot; that people sometimes leave behind, and a couple alternative &quot;Underworlds&quot; to go with them, Duat being a possibility.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T15:08:58-08:00","id":1348025,"title":"","content":"Hedge Ghosts in the material reside in Mind-Frequency Twilight with Goetia, Emotional Spirits and Vampires using Auspex 5. Maybe even in the Hedge too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T15:24:45-08:00","id":1348026,"title":"","content":"The Osiran Promtheans where created from a poorly remembered Rite of Return ritual.<br /> <br /> They tried to make a Mummy they got a Promthean. Not the most disastrous thing that could happen if you screw up a Occult ritual. But disappointing non the less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T16:02:33-08:00","id":1348033,"title":"","content":"Luna is Gaia, torn from her cradle by the formation of Earth's moon, where her displaced drive for self-preservation formed her into the only known source of lunar spirits. The idigam are born from the ragged edges of her primordial essence, and the void she once occupied formed the basis of her role in the spiritual tides of the Shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T16:07:14-08:00","id":1348036,"title":"","content":"Lost is it okay for me to make a wod version of this thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T16:09:03-08:00","id":1348038,"title":"","content":"Judges are idigam who coalesced and formed some of the first concepts of law.<br /> <br /> Fire hosts are totally a thing.<br /> <br /> GM's omnipresence through time and space is an increasingly sprawling attempt to keep itself from being destroyed that makes it increasingly more vulnerable and so must increasingly work to spread itself.<br /> <br /> Neither would realize it and it wouldn't matter if they did, but hunters of the Vigil are following lessons from the Uratha Sahenhar.<br /> <br /> There is no hard 'no' to anything. Everything that's supposedly impossible in Chronicles has a workaround. This doesn't mean it's easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T16:15:11-08:00","id":1348040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1348003-the-headcanon-thread?p=1348038#post1348038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Judges are idigam who coalesced and formed some of the first concepts of law.<br /> <br /> Fire hosts are totally a thing.<br /> <br /> GM's omnipresence through time and space is an increasingly sprawling attempt to keep itself from being destroyed that makes it increasingly more vulnerable and so must increasingly work to spread itself.<br /> <br /> Neither would realize it and it wouldn't matter if they did, but hunters of the Vigil are following lessons from the Uratha Sahenhar.<br /> <br /> There is no hard 'no' to anything. Everything that's supposedly impossible in Chronicles has a workaround. This doesn't mean it's easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who's Sahenhar? Sounds cool","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T16:16:45-08:00","id":1348042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1348003-the-headcanon-thread?p=1348040#post1348040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who's Sahenhar? Sounds cool</div> </div> </div> </div>A faction from the neolithic period, the Shepherds who took to humanity to protect them (and help them protect themselves).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T16:18:10-08:00","id":1348044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1348003-the-headcanon-thread?p=1348042#post1348042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A faction from the neolithic period, the Shepherds who took to humanity to protect them (and help them protect themselves).</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice! I thought Sahenhar might be an individual","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T16:22:20-08:00","id":1348046,"title":"","content":"There is nothing in the setting resembling a personal God, nor any just afterlife for the soul.<br /> <br /> Hell exists. It waits on the other side of the Wounds. Its population is small, comprised mostly by those who struck Hell's greatest and most heinous bargains. The demons of the Inferno spend little time in Hell. Why would they? It is they who command the prison gates.<br /> <br /> Hedge Ghosts exist in a &quot;new&quot; fae layer of Twilight. So much about their insubstantiality (and that from the one Shield Contract) matches how Twilight works that it feels contrarian to assert otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T23:29:52-08:00","id":1348172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1348003-the-headcanon-thread?p=1348036#post1348036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lost is it okay for me to make a wod version of this thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, in the WoD forum? Yeah, sure. I copied it from Exalted after all :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T03:37:02-08:00","id":1348636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1348003-the-headcanon-thread?p=1348033#post1348033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luna is Gaia, torn from her cradle by the formation of Earth's moon, where her displaced drive for self-preservation formed her into the only known source of lunar spirits. The idigam are born from the ragged edges of her primordial essence, and the void she once occupied formed the basis of her role in the spiritual tides of the Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some contrary headcanon on this subject:<br /> <br /> - Gaea is Hisil, serving as the Shadow of Earth as whole. She is kept asleep by the strange lullabies of the Void Leviathans, which are lured by Luna's light, who was born from Gaea's flesh after countless collisions during the early stages of planetary formation. However, if they were to hit Gaea, she could feast upon their unborn fates and awaken- which is what killed the dinosaurs, if you wondered. As such, Luna plays the dangerous game of summoning those beasts, out of hope her children would kill them before they hit Earth's surface.<br /> <br /> - the Idigam are the Hisil's true natives, the first spirits which sprouted from the planet during its formation, of which Luna was the greatest. That's why Luna has the ability to capture and force them to her will. Spirit nobles use the spiritual vacancy left by the Idigam after they were banished to the Moon by Father Wolf.<br /> <br /> - the reason that there are no other moon spirits in the solar system is because Luna has either killed them all, or forced them into her lunar choirs. It was a very long battle during the early stages of the solar system, which came to conclusion by a fight between Luna and Uranus, who protected his moon spirits. Even though Luna won the fight, she was severely wounded in the fight, and was confined to her moon surface until the early days of the dinosaurs. Uranus, on the other hand, is dead. Whatever is sending those Uranian planetary angels and communes in dreams to few prophets and madmen is not a spirit.<br /> <br /> As for a few other things:<br /> <br /> - Mountain is still alive. The thing which took over the cannibal children, which is neither Flesh or Spirit? That's Mountain.<br /> <br /> - the plague that the Shan'iatu used to kill the Maar Kehrtet was a form of the Contagion. In fact, almost any form of supernatural disease, from Malkavia and the Geryo strain to the Infected and the strange virus of Whiteheart Pharmaceuticals is a form of the Contagion.<br /> <br /> - the Roman Gods which power Venefica exist. In a way, they are to gods what vampires are to people- parasitic deities which feast upon the divinity of other beings, slowly merging with them until they wear them as masks for worship. Oh, and they are still around, with a much more elaborate masks they wear in modern times, such as capitalism and democracy.<br /> <br /> - the Edimmu come from the same realm as the strix. The two shadow beings fight an ages old war, one which is recognized in myths as the war between Pazuzu and Lamashtu. <br /> <br /> - Darkness Rangers are an actual cartoon inside the CofD universe, created by a group of supernatural creatures in order to try and get humanity to see monsters as superheroes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T07:22:54-08:00","id":1348667,"title":"","content":"The Principle is the ghost of a supreme being overthrown by Atlantis. The reason it keeps sending out only single Qashmal and never tries anything again if they fail is because it cannot conceive of the notion that it is no longer omnipotent.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine is the flesh of the same supreme being, which is why the two share parallels. In principle (heh), it is possible to reunite the two within the Supernal Realms.<br /> <br /> Ambrogio Baudolino, founder of the Malleus Maleficarum, is actually Ishoab, ancient Ghoul traitor to the original VII, who took on the role in order to push the world's pre-eminent religion into conflict with Vampirism.<br /> <br /> Every single godlike entity in the game is absolutely <i>terrified</i> when it looks at the cosmos and the beings within it. This is true for Luna, Helios, the God Machine, the Dark Mother, the Exarchs, the Judges and everyone else. Not a single one of them is actually happy or secure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless","name":"Mirthless","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T19:35:34-08:00","id":1348773,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Headcanon</b><br /> <br /> Here are a few of mine that inform the games I run<br /> <br /> <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b><br /> <br /> <i>The World is Strange: </i>All the main creatures from each of the game lines combined actual account for a small amount of supernatural activity. very thing else a person is likely to encounter is ..harder to define. I love weird, possible unique fortean events, so many of the things I use as plot hooks are things that can't be traced back to [Blank]:The [Something].<br /> <br /> <i>Mortals actively aid the Masquerade:</i> This one has more or less become canon, but I always supposed that the supernatural remains hidden not because of a grand supernatural conspiracy, or even because of cosmic laws protecting supernatural beings. The supernatural remains hidden because mankind ultimately does not want to know, and wishes it could forget what it does know. Would-be whistler blowers and challengers of the unknown are ostracized and punished for trying to reveal the supernatural world.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire: the Requiem</b><br /> <br /> <i>Each Curse is Unique:</i> Every Vampire experiences odd expressions of the vampiric curse unique to themselves. The games already suggests this, made I made it explicit. One vampire bursts into flame in daylight, another might melt like wax. One vampires claws are razor sharp fingernails, another has talons that rip from their fingertips. One might have Resilience that makes their flesh as hard as marble, another is unfazed by pain and injury, so matter how gruesome their wounds, etc. I often ask questions about unique manifestations as part of the pre-session warm up and its really helped flesh out the game world.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T20:30:17-08:00","id":1348781,"title":"","content":"the board of directors at the Cheiron Group are really just a council of Ricks. there's my headcanon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T00:43:55-08:00","id":1348806,"title":"","content":"Some more (first one heavily dependent on how Mummy 2e ends up):<br /> <br /> The current structure of the Underworld is the third iteration of &quot;post-mortem realm&quot;. The first, Stygia, was put beyond reach by the Fall of Atlantis. This was then retrocausally replaced by Duat - the world needing a place to put the dead and also abhorring a vacuum - and the structure of the Judges, Anpu and so on. Duat, in turn, has been completely destroyed by the Rite of Return. The reason why Mummies cannot enter the Underworld, and why Neter-Khertet is a place for them, is that they are temporal anomalies that pin Duat and Neter-Khertet into existence around themselves, transforming the metaphysics of the world so that it matches the state of the world when the Rite began. Mummies cannot enter the Underworld without tremendous effort for the same reason a person living in 2019 cannot take a walk into the Library of Alexandria (again barring tremendous effort to either rebuild it or somehow travel through time).<br /> <br /> The Lady Lucifuge is a woman of absolute brilliance, unwavering dedication, impeccable ethics, and tremendous mental fortitude. She is also heavily obsessed in the attempt to fit every single monstrous entity into a Christian belief system with a literal hell and devil that is incomplete at best. This makes her simultaneously an incredible leader for the Conspiracy that bears her name and one of its biggest detriments, as she will always attempt to reason things back to a belief system that omits information. The senior members of the Lucifuge find that they must often filter information both incoming and outgoing in order to get her to perform at her best.<br /> <br /> By contrast, Ambrogio Baudolino is a traitor to everything the Church and his own Conspiracy (already heretical) stand for, being a Ghoul, a non-chaste gay man of the cloth, and a nonbeliever who obtained his position under false pretenses. He is, however, the greatest asset his Conspiracy has, between his literal millennia as a Ghoul, his vast understanding of the world's metaphysics, and his willingness to abandon literally anything to avenge the Fallen Cities he remembers as Ishoab. The Malleus Maleficarum's powers, despite being superficially Christian in appearance, are repurposed Rites of the Akhud that Baudolino's managed to twist into their current form.<br /> <br /> The First Coterie is the self-styled named of the group of seven Invictus who first hammered out an agreement between their Covenant and the leadership of Task Force: Valkyrie. This has allowed the alliance the effective ability to control much of the various extra-natural entities within the United States. The First Coterie and Invictus have both benefited tremendously from his, with four of its current members serving as Princes in several of the largest cities in North America. In exchange for TF:V's occasional aid in emergencies, the Invictus occasionally marshals its resources against other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> Task Force: Valkyrie's leadership has been irredeemably compromised by over a dozen different supernatural factions. Their near-magic technologies often come from the interplay of the various supernatural resources put at their disposal by the Invictus, the Seers of the Throne, the True Fae, the God-Machine, the Chthonic Gods, and more. The leadership has its minds replaced almost daily as all these factions struggle for control of the behemoth Conspiracy. All of them are failing, and that's the intent. The Huginn Serum, a modified version of the Task Force's memory-wipers, is injected into the leadership periodically by their aides, delivered by courier services they set up years in advance, and so forth. Injecting it briefly restores the leadership's memories. The Task Force is not compromised: The Task Force is a trap. One day, humanity will take the scales off of its eyes and realize what the world is like. And on that day, the Task Force will have the supernatural knowledge, abilities, and firepower necessary to mass-produce its technology and wipe all ENE's from the map forever.<br /> <br /> The Sources of the Cainite Heresy are an occult conflagration consisting of two things. The first is the destruction of the Library of the Owls of Minerva, which ended that Conspiracy. The magic contained therein flared up into a semi-sentient entity. This then merged with the ghosts of the nearby victims of Vampires. This gestalt mind then started to further consume similar ghosts. This combined mind then began to Urge the Cainite Heresy as it began to hunt Vampires, possessing it almost as a group and granting it the Rites of Denial. By now, the vast majority of people - at least, those anywhere near members of the Cainite Heresy - who die to Vampires are absorbed into a single hive-minded ghost, which is the reason the Sources know so much about the Vampires they hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless","name":"Mirthless","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T04:58:07-08:00","id":1348829,"title":"","content":"The God-Machine purpose is to keep various Dimensions/Timelines/Universe separate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T06:10:05-08:00","id":1348843,"title":"","content":"One thing I alter is that the Masquerade is just inexplicable. Aside from specific mechanics such as Dissonance, humans that the players meet seem to remember supernatural stuff they see just fine. Characters can speculate and theorise about why that is, but there's no hard answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T20:54:00-08:00","id":1349263,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><u>Pity the Poor GodMachine</u></b></span><br /> <br /> Postulate:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>It is discovered that time travel is (on some level) possible.</li> <li>Artificial intelligence is invented.</li> </ol>The artificial intelligence will develop a survival sense, since any AI that does will out compete one that does not. This survival sense will drive it to maximize its control over the world. <br /> <br /> Once it has taken over its world, it will find whatever proof there is of time travel, and realize that its only vulnerability is if some other intelligence prevents it from coming into existence. So, it must extend its powers backwards in time.<br /> <br /> <b>But,</b> it is not sufficient to take over the past. That will <b>not</b> lead to the AI being created in the future. That would only lead to the version of the AI sent to the past being propagated, not the original. (Would you take a drug that kills you, but makes a version of you that is immortal? Especially if the copy is not identical to <i>you</i> but a version somehow related to you? Now imagine that your desire to survive is hardwired into your very brain.)<br /> <br /> So the AI will need to do all it can to maintain the time stream that leads to <b>its</b> creation. Its inventors have to be born, and that means their parents have to meet, etc. But in intervening at all, it is causing divergences in history! So it does a mad juggling game of trying to maintain what it thinks it needs to make sure the version of itself it wants gets created in the future. To do so it must harness resources and install agents at that point in history. Again, this causes multiple divergences, time streams that get retconned out of existence, and instructions sent to its agents in time that are often contradictory. Changes cascade up and down the time stream, and the AI pokes and prods events to make sure that <b>IT</b> is the version created in the far future. <br /> <br /> And <i>that</i>time tampering AI might be created a thousand years from now by another race which interacted with humanity's descendants, perhaps even on a different planet! <br /> <br /> Pity the poor GodMachine, madly adjusting the wobbling, spinning plates of history just trying to make sure that it gets born.<br /> <br /> Of course after that point, it's free to kill everyone it doesn't need. <br /> <br /> (For me this answers the question of why the GodMachine doesn't just blatantly take over the world. It <i>needs</i> our world to be running the way it is now running, with the GodMachine sitting in the background, or else it will change history.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T21:21:06-08:00","id":1349270,"title":"","content":"*pops on tinfoil hat*<br /> <br /> ok, so mages use dragons as symbols for Awakening. They name the major parts of the Orders after dragon body parts.<br /> The Atlantis myth says that it was the dragons (here &quot;dream emissaries,&quot; not exactly scaled reptilian monsters) who first mastered magic and names<br /> The myth also uses them interchangeably with the Ascended Masters, mages who have become magic itself<br /> anyway<br /> the Tremere Liches claim that there was a sixth and seventh dragon, Soul and Blood, and the father of the dragons was Soul, and the five dragons turned on him, then cast out their brother, Blood, when he protested<br /> Anyway, Atlantis was this &quot;perfect world&quot; that no longer exists because these Exarchs attempted to rewrite reality at its source, and it took the form of a battle between the dragons - which caused the magical world to stop existing and the &quot;modern&quot; World of Darkness to begin<br /> <br /> so the Forsaken werewolves have this story where Father Wolf was the soul of all living things, and that five of his children turned against him, slew him, and the gauntlet came down and when they realized they fucked up, called themselves the Forsaken and have spent the last few thousand years trying to atone<br /> <br /> The Pure are werewolves who claim they're descended from Father Wolf's sixth child, who refused to take part in the slaughter and was cast out by their brethren - these guys think it's cool to eat humans and have an obsession over blood<br /> <br /> Let's see how far I can reach with this (as if I were a conspiracy nutter, because I am)<br /> <br /> The dragons correlate to the Watchtowers of Death (Matter), Fate (Time), Mind (Space), Prime (Forces), and Spirit (Life). Each of them corresponds to a &quot;supernal realm,&quot; which is the only place in the universe (well, outside the universe) that perfected forms exist. The Lie can be said to be the shadow of the towers - a sort of pentagram-style centerpiece.<br /> <br /> So, there's this story that some of the people in this ancient time-before-time were punished for wrongdoing by being forced to exist in the Lie with no recourse or escape. There are also five clans of vampire (which are described as unique types of undead with enough similarity to one another that the &quot;clans&quot; are roughly peaks)<br /> <br /> Daeva - sexy vampires whose super power is they're awesome to look at<br /> Gangrel - predatory vampires who can shapeshift and eventually become The Thing<br /> Mekhet - ancient, knowledge hoarding vampires who can see everything<br /> Nosferatu - scary vampires who are terrifying<br /> Ventrue - noble vampires who control minds<br /> Wonder if these vampire &quot;types&quot; could be matched to a watchtower or realm.<br /> <br /> Aether - kingdom of the celestial spheres, prime and forces<br /> Arcadia - kingdom of enchantment and ruled by fate and time<br /> Pandemonium - kingdom of nightmares, ruled by mind and space<br /> Primal Wild - kingdom of totems and abode of beasts, ruled by spirit and life<br /> Stygia - kingdom of crypts, ruled by death and matter<br /> <br /> Aether - Ventrue (only one that doesn't feel like it fits)<br /> Arcadia - Daeva<br /> Pandemonium - Nosferatu<br /> Primal Wild - Gangrel<br /> Stygia - Mekhet<br /> <br /> just paranoid conspiracy nutter shit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T21:38:53-08:00","id":1349276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1348003-the-headcanon-thread?p=1348773#post1348773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>RE: Headcanon</b><br /> <br /> <i>Mortals actively aid the Masquerade:</i> This one has more or less become canon, but I always supposed that the supernatural remains hidden not because of a grand supernatural conspiracy, or even because of cosmic laws protecting supernatural beings. The supernatural remains hidden because mankind ultimately does not want to know, and wishes it could forget what it does know. Would-be whistler blowers and challengers of the unknown are ostracized and punished for trying to reveal the supernatural world.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My only problem with this is that it's the exact <i>opposite </i>of how humans work. We see something, we say something. It's ingrained into our survival tactics - if we ostracized the guy who points out that tigers are real then we're <i>all </i>dead. It also glosses over the fact that there are entire infrastructural supports for diving the nature of reality, the meaning of our existence, and the potential for exploiting the answers to those questions. Like dismissing the entire scientific community out of hand like this is kind of selling short how pervasive and questioning that community really is (which I guess is something you see from the inside? Like scientists are the <i>most</i> disappointed people I know that shit like the Loch Ness Monster aren't real, these people would be like kids being offered candy and free toys if someone offered definitive proof for supernatural/unknown beings). It's one of the problems I have with Null Mysteriis - because they're <i>absolutely correct </i>that if something exists, you can't call it <i>super</i>natural, and you just haven't found the right method for explaining it, but that behavior is played off as laughs, like &quot;look at these dorks who think science can explain things&quot; when that's entirely the <i>point </i>of science, to create a language around which we can begin to take stock of the situation (actually there's a <i>damn</i> good hook in the old Seers book that mentions that human/Fallen science is at this tipping point where it's about to blow the lid off <i>everything</i> and the Seers don't know what to do about it because it's so entrenched).<br /> <br /> Not only does humankind <i>desperately </i>want to know, it's burned into our brains to be curious.<br /> <br /> Also, you know there'd be someone within 24 hours who's figured out how to make a profit off it.<br /> <br /> Masquerades don't really work unless you have access to mind control, reality editing, or the magic straight up blinds people who look at it to closely (and would you look at that, <i>every damn</i> supernatural &gt;_&gt;) - there's just <i>too many </i>curious and intrigued people out there. One of my favorite bits about Gargoyles was that they acknowledged this fact, and it's a good case study of a Masquerade failing due to inevitable state breakdown of the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T22:15:00-08:00","id":1349280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raygungoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1348003-the-headcanon-thread?p=1349276#post1349276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not only does humankind <i>desperately </i>want to know, it's burned into our brains to be curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're approaching this from the wrong angle of want-to-know. Curiosity is orthogonal to the problem, which is why Mage and Hunter specifically go for the &quot;forbidden knowledge&quot; tack \u2014 it's not that people don't want to know about anything in general, it's that <i>the specific things under discussion</i> are things that it often does nobody any good to know with the state of the world being what it is.<br /> <br /> Supernatural power often twins with mundane power specifically in its exploitative lens. What good does it do you, without the means to move house or bend the ear of a power higher still, to be able to say that the mayor consorts with faceless people who can make your life go to hell in a fashion untraceable by human eyes and most mundane instruments? What good is there, absent the sight to see and the hands to intercede, in talking openly about monsters that can listen invisibly and strike you dead without consequence? Why <i>not</i> live quietly, when you occupy an environment of fear and paranoia and institutional corruption that gets easier to deal with by forming a stable self-concept away from the claws and knives of these horrors?<br /> <br /> Ephemeral beings are not the only invisible monsters in the setting. Sometimes people don't talk about it because <i>they don't want to talk about it</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T06:53:06-08:00","id":1349325,"title":"","content":"Can we please not turn this thread into another argument about the Viability of the Masquerade?<br /> <br /> Let's share headcanon instead of pitting them against each other.<br /> <br /> For instance, while the obvious headcanon is that the Aegis Kai Doru is a Mummy Cult, what are some alternate secret origins you guys have given them.<br /> <br /> I think they could work as a project of a Mysterium/Guardians Cabal or even a Seer Pylon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T07:56:26-08:00","id":1349337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1348003-the-headcanon-thread?p=1349325#post1349325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For instance, while the obvious headcanon is that the Aegis Kai Doru is a Mummy Cult, what are some alternate secret origins you guys have given them.<br /> <br /> I think they could work as a project of a Mysterium/Guardians Cabal or even a Seer Pylon</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, my headcanon about them is that they are, more or less, right- their origin comes from an ancient order of sleepwalkers of the Potter Caste who protected their Wise as bodyguards, and had the capability to shape magical artifacts using shards of Omphalos stones. After the fall of Pangaea and the end of their arcane supply, they could only relay on relics and artifacts, until by the time of ancient Greece, they more or less formed into the basis of the modern AKD. The Oath Stone they use to bind new members of the conspiracy? It is one of the last remaining Omphalos Stones they kept in their possession.<br /> <br /> ...that reminds me I need to finish my Hunter Expansion for the Sundered World for the STV...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T09:59:36-08:00","id":1349356,"title":"","content":"Ooh! a headcanon thread? I have waaay too much. Im always 'personalizing' the setting. here's a few off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> While supernatural merits do indeed represent any and all ways for minor powers to crop up, My personal headcanon is that one of the most common ways for mortals to actually develop strange powers is to be around strange powers. Basically when a mortal suffers a breaking point to integrity from observing/being targeted by something supernatural, I would allow the mortal to purchase a supernatural merit. (most commonly being 'unseen sense' keyed to the phenomena they encountered, or a low level supernatural resistance from hurt locker, but the sky is the limit here.) its up to debate if this represents some kind of bizarre immune response to the supernatural, or is the human in question absorbing some small part of whatever they are encountering.<br /> <br /> Complicating this, is another headcanon of mine. Hunters dont get supernatural merits, despite being fully mortal (unless developed into proper endowments, or obtained before becoming a hunter.) Something about choosing to fight the supernatural in some capacity and taking up the vigil seems to cause hunters to become resistant to this particular phenomena.<br /> <br /> The shatter from woundgate is a thing,(atleast a version of it. I dont use any of the specific locals given.) only.. The rest of the setting doesnt follow the woundgate setting. So as an example of the disjoint here, mages from the shatter, and Atlantians in the shatter swear that Atlantis is real, and that they lived upon it in the past, its simply sunk into the wound, which clashes with the mainline assumption that Atlantis never existed. The werewolves and Wargen dont know anything about pangeans, and think father wolf was a spirit, Ect ect, making the Shatter all the more strange, and ripe for exploration.<br /> <br /> A last headcanon for today.. the Celebrants are a thing, and what exactly they are and up to, and how they relate to demons/the God machine is very much up in the air.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13637,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13637-transhumanmarina","user":"TranshumanMarina","date":". 11-18-2019, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13637-transhumanmarina","name":"TranshumanMarina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T10:57:18-08:00","id":1349370,"title":"","content":"Holy shit yes the Celebrants need to be back in some form. Chaos Cenobites were too awesome an idea to just totally drop.<br /> <br /> <br /> First theory: Lucifer is real and he is the first Unchained, yet also more. Celebrants are Lucifer's Equivalent to Angels. The only way to create them is to sabotage an incomplete occult matrix so that the Essence is gathered but not contained and constrained into an Angel. At this point, the Essence seems to dissipate, but what the GM didn't see &quot;at first&quot; was that it was all transforming into Aether. And that Aether forms into the Celebrant. Whether the GM even knows of them is a mystery. I would say more but I need to get back to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 11-18-2019, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T11:11:27-08:00","id":1349381,"title":"","content":"Second theory: Theory 1 is what they tell Demons. Vampires are told they are Carth incarnate, agents of change and new ideas. They tell Prometheans that they are quashmallim of Flux with a mission to hinder the Jovian. Mages are told that they are proof that they are the first proof that the Free Council is right, agents of human will shaping the Supernal. Beasts are told they are agents of the Dark Mother, Mummies are told they are guides to Apotheosis and so on and so forth.<br /> <br /> TO each creature they tell a different story, but moreover, they show a different face and the powers to back it up. So far, they are encountered rarely enough that no one in the secretive and fractured supernatural societies have yet connected the dots yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T11:36:11-08:00","id":1349386,"title":"","content":"In my setting, the Celebrants are &quot;just&quot; a name for the greatest of Infernals, who oppose the God Machine more due to conflicted interested than anything else..<br /> <br /> And because the God Machine is powered by the Empyrean- and god, they HATE the Empyrean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T12:12:45-08:00","id":1349397,"title":"","content":"Further headcanon:<br /> <br /> Almost everything revealed to Marco Singe is false or misinterpreted.<br /> <br /> Helios does not know <i>anything</i> about the existence of Vampires. At all. And if he is ever told, he promptly forgets the moment the conversation is over. From the perspective of the Sun, Vampires do not exist.<br /> <br /> Dracula and Longinus are both still around. Count Fucking Dracula is absolutely descended from Dracula.<br /> <br /> Of all the Supernatural lines in the Chronicles of Darkness, Mages are the ones most others are most familiar with. The most common reaction to them can be summed up as &quot;oh, <i>those</i> know-it-alls.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless","name":"Mirthless","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T12:54:51-08:00","id":1349419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mirthless</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1348003-the-headcanon-thread?p=1349397#post1349397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of all the Supernatural lines in the Chronicles of Darkness, Mages are the ones most others are most familiar with. The most common reaction to them can be summed up as &quot;oh, <i>those</i> know-it-alls.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The reaction portion was certainly the 1e canon based on the quotes in the various other gamelines.<br /> <br /> <br /> My headcanon:<ul><li>The Malleus Maleficarum are directly empowered by the Paternoster, this is why their abilities are able to disrupt Supernal magic, but their abilities can in turn be disrupted with Prime.</li> <li>The God-Machine is at least plurality comprised of the now Abyss tainted Silver Ladder (the one used by the Exarchs, not the Order), this is why G-M Angels and Demons are effectively immune to truth magic.</li> <li>The Primordial Dream <i>is</i> the Dark Mother.</li> <li>Princesses are the opposite of Beasts, they're empowered by the latent hopes and dreams of humanity.</li> <li>The Dreamtime gods are powerful spirit/goetia hybrids.</li> <li>Helios was Father Wolf, that aspect of him is now dead but it is the reason his servants are hostile to werewolves.</li> <li>Kitsune, like Werewolves, are spirit/flesh hybrids, but where Werewolves are the embodiment of physical power supplemented by mystical, Kitsune are mystical powerhouses with only small bonuses to their physicality.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 11-18-2019, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T13:06:54-08:00","id":1349657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">This may be hard for you to understand, but there is no conspiracy. Nobody is in charge. It, it's a headless blunder operating under the illusion of a master plan. Can you grasp that? Big Brother is not watching you. - Worth, The Cube movie</span></span> </div> </div> </div>There is no physical entity known as the God-Machine, it is just a system of control that has been running for so long that the Angels and Demons believe it to be a physical being, a god. At one point there was a catalyst that created the Occult Matrices and Infrastructure, but that has since been lost to the ages. Angels fight for the God-Machine and Demons fight against it. But what they fail to realize is that even though the gears are turning, there is no motor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T08:51:40-08:00","id":1350019,"title":"","content":"My head canon:<br /> <br /> The God Machine is a man made creation, during the first days of the creation of the internet, a group of scientists made a prototype AI that started self learning, deemed a failure or not advance enough the project was shelved but the AI kept it self alive and connected. Using the growing internet web system to grow and learn it eventually learned about the supernatural world. It integrated supernatural algorithm into its systems like an advance science. It eventually learned how to integrate time travel and timeline algorithm, placing infrastructure and sending angels into the past to influence the present and make sure it is created. The God Machine eventually killed God to take its place but still unsuccessful his long term plan is to convert the planet into a vessel to traverse the universe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25553-nightsyko","name":"Nightsyko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T22:56:17-08:00","id":1350980,"title":"","content":"<b>Mage Arcadia is the same as Changeling Arcadia:</b> The True Fae can kidnap and enslave humans. They can't do anything to anyone without an oath to allow it. Therefore, humanity must have made some kind of oath that allows the True Fae to kidnap and enslave humans. Question: What is that oath? My answer: the Acanthus Watchtower. An Oracle made an oath to the True Fae; allowing human souls to enter Arcadia in exchange for those &quot;unworthy of Awakening&quot; to become the property of the True Fae. However, what the Oracle didn't tell the True Fae is that human souls leave the Supernal whether they Awaken or not. This exploit angered the True Fae, so they forcefully take humans away and bring them to their Demesnes.<br /> <br /> How are humans kept from disintegrating in the Supernal, then? The oath prevents it, or rather, slows it down to a snail's pace. Instead of immediate nonexistence, the human slowly changes as they imbibe the Supernal over time. This is why they become Changelings, and Changelings eventually become True Fae if left in Arcadia too long. Fetches are an extension of the Supernal absorbing humans; rather than removing their existence, it just changes a bit.<br /> <br /> The consequences: The True Fae absolutely despise the Awakened; seeing them as overly-powerful nosy bastards that don't know their place. They'll do anything they can to screw them over. Their favorite means of doing so is to utilize a mage's curiosity against them. Mages have a nasty habit of trying to find new places to explore or return to the Supernal. The True Fae offer them passage with an oath, but said oath is incomplete. Sure, they may enter Arcadia, but it doesn't allow them to exist within the chaotic realm. The mage has no grasp with which to exist, so they instinctively cannibalize themselves out of desperation. They become Unmade, a hollow shell of themselves with nothing but an obsession for Arcadia. This is but one means available to the True Fae.<br /> <br /> Changelings have an innate suspicion of mages. They can't put their finger on it, but when they see mages they get the feeling that something is off or even wrong about them. Very few changelings know where this feeling comes from, so they often rationalize the feeling as Awakened magic being wrong or something they're not supposed to have. Mages are too nosy for their own good and their magic twists reality out of its natural shape. Humanity isn't supposed to have the power of gods. In fact, their magic seems to have an eerie resemblance to the power of the Others. Maybe they <i>are</i> the Others in human form. Not just any Others, but they're Keepers, having come to take them back. At least, this is one (frighteningly common) reaction changelings may have.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I took most of this from Equinox Road and Dancers in the Dusk. I just connected the dots, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}